# Labelled cases for the inbox-triage rubric. Each case labels the questions
# it is sure about; a question left out is asked and not graded.
jud: 1.2
kind: cases
id: inbox-triage-cases
rubric: inbox-triage
description: Seven messages, labelled by the support lead on 2026-10-04.

cases:
  - id: refund-angry
    state:
      message: >-
        This is the third time I'm writing. I was charged twice last month and
        nobody has refunded me. Fix it today or I cancel.
    expect:
      actionable: true
      desk: billing
      tone: angry
    tags: [billing, repeat]

  - id: thanks
    state:
      message: Sorted now, thanks a lot for the quick help!
    expect:
      actionable: false
      desk: none_of_these
      tone: calm

  - id: login-loop
    state:
      message: >-
        After the update I get sent back to the sign-in page every time I log
        in. Cleared cookies, same thing. Chrome on a Mac.
    expect:
      actionable: true
      desk: technical
      tone: annoyed

  - id: receipt
    state:
      message: >-
        Your payment of 12.00 EUR was received. This is an automated message,
        please do not reply.
    expect:
      actionable: false
      desk: none_of_these
    tags: [automated]
    note: the Noul is the hard one here; the message is about billing but asks nothing

  - id: close-account
    state:
      message: Please close my account and delete my data. Thanks.
    expect:
      actionable: true
      desk: account
      tone: 0

  - id: how-to-export
    state:
      message: Is there a way to export my data as CSV? Could not find it in settings.
    expect:
      actionable: true
      desk: technical
      tone: calm

  - id: invoice-vat
    state:
      message: Can you reissue last month's invoice with our VAT number on it?
    expect:
      actionable: true
      desk: billing
      tone: calm
